WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.850
- Welcome to the Huberman Lab Podcast,

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.890
where we discuss science
and science based tools

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:05.933
for everyday life.

00:00:07.056 --> 00:00:09.310
[upbeat rock music]

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:10.250
I'm Andrew Huberman,

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.930
and I'm a professor of
neurobiology and ophthalmology

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.890
at Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.270
Today, my guest is Dr. Paul Conti.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.840
Dr. Conti is a psychiatrist

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.330
who did his training at
Stanford School of Medicine,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.970
and then went on to be chief resident

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.320
at Harvard Medical School.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.360
He now runs the Pacific Premier Group,

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.830
which is a collection of
psychiatrists and therapists

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.530
focusing on solving
complex human problems,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.040
including trauma, addiction, personality,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.970
and psychiatric disorders.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.380
Today, we discuss trauma in detail

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.910
and the therapeutic process in detail.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.320
For instance, we discuss what is trauma?

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.450
How do you know if you have trauma?

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.340
Dr. Conti shares with us, for instance,

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.590
that not every experience
that we think is traumatic

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:50.950
is necessarily traumatic

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.350
and yet many people might have trauma

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.810
without even realizing it.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.310
We also talk about the
therapeutic process generally,

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.170
for instance, how to pick a therapist,

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.500
how to best approach
and go through therapy

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.600
and how to evaluate whether or not therapy

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.460
and your relationship to the
therapist is working or not.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.120
We also talk about self
therapies because we acknowledge

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.630
that not everyone has access
to or can afford therapy.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.900
And we talk about drug therapies,

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.920
for instance, antidepressants,
antipsychotics.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.500
We talk about alcohol, cannabis,

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.840
ketamine and the psychedelics,
including psilocybin, LSD.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.420
And we talk about the clinical use of MDMA

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.210
and what the future of that looks like.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.680
The reason for bringing
Dr. Conti onto this podcast

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.210
is because I see him as the person

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:38.260
who has the greatest and most
holistic view of therapy,

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.180
trauma, drug therapies, talk therapies,

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.520
and how self therapy and work
with others can be integrated

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.860
for both healing and growing
from difficult circumstances.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.810
Dr. Conti is also the author
of an exceptional book,

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.520
entitled "Trauma: The Invisible Epidemic,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.460
How trauma works and how
we can heal from it."

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.930
That book describes trauma

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.740
and its many features and many tools,

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.330
some of which we discuss
on the podcast today.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:06.110
So whether or not you have trauma or not,

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.350
by the end of today's episode,

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.170
you will have a much deeper understanding

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.750
about what trauma is.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.770
In fact, I'm confident
that you will gain insight

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.010
into whether or not
you have trauma or not,

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.290
whether or not people close
to you have trauma or not

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:20.130
and the various paths to
recovering and indeed growing

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.390
from trauma that we can all take.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:23.910
As you'll soon learn Dr. Conti

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.490
is an exceptional communicator
and has a unique window

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.740
into the trauma and therapeutic process

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.210
that I know that all
of us can benefit from.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.043
Before we begin,

00:02:33.043 --> 00:02:35.270
I'd like to emphasize that
this podcast is separate

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.500
